A Boeing Flight Operations Bulletin, dated July 13, 2001, stated, "Several MD-80/B717 operators have reported incidents of Nose Landing Gear (NLG) spray deflector damage occurring when taxing or operating over rigid military arresting gear."&#x0D;
&#x0D;
Subsequent to the accident, a Boeing Flight Operations Bulletin, dated September 20, 2001, stated:&#x0D;
	The purpose of this revision is to clarify and broaden the scope of this operations &#x0D;
	bulletin, to include possible damage to the NLG SPRAY DEFLECTOR caused &#x0D;
	by taxiing over a chock, striking a taxiway light or other obstruction, dropping the &#x0D;
