At the time of the accident, America West Airlines had its headquarters in Phoenix, Arizona, and operated 104 airplanes, including 1 Boeing 737-100, 17 Boeing 737-200, 44 Boeing 737-300, 13 Boeing 757-200, 21 Airbus A-320-231, and 8 A-320-232 airplanes.  The company employed 1,425 pilots and 298 certificated mechanics, and holds Air Carrier Operating Certificate Number AWXA420A.&#x0D;
